  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Strengthen LP in apparel industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To address these emerging challenges of the Cambodian textile and garment sector that especially (female) garment workers in the informal sector are confronted with and in line with the European&#x2019;s due diligence law, it is critical that knowledge and awareness about labour rights and unionisation amongst (female) workers in sub-contract factories are built and strengthened. And by having access to capacity building including training and unionisation opportunity, network building and dialogue space workers will be confidence, acquire knowledge, and built the courage to demand for their rights and entitlement to decent working condition, labour rights and protection, and their accessibility and entitlement to recent social protection schemes &#x2013;NSSF and pension fund.
Oxfam proposes the following initiative: &#x201c;Improved Access to Labor Protection Mechanisms and Gender Equality for Female Workers in the Apparel Sectorin CambodiaXXX&#x201d;. The primary objective of this project is to contribute to improved labourlabor rights,  gender equality for femaleapparel industry workers and social protection schemes. Specifically, Oxfam envisions the following objectives:
&#x2022; Capacity development of unions to better represent and negotiate workers&#x2019; rights and thus prepare the grounds for improved labour rights, better complaint structures and freedom of association,
&#x2022; Improved knowledge and awareness of (female) garment workers in informal factories onlabour rights (e.g. social protection, pension, maternity leave) and freedom of association and strengthened leadership and soft skills of female garment workers to engage in social dialogues and negotiations to demand their rights,
&#x2022; Provide safe space for unionisation in informal factories.

And Oxfam in Cambodia will partner with Coalition of Cambodian Apparel Workers Democratic Union (C.CAWDU) in terms of technical support, national and regional advocacy platform, and other policy influencing work involving unionisation, labour rights and social protection, and human rights due diligence in Cambodia&apos;s apparel industry.</narrative>
  </description>
